## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical application of cache-aside in CNPA, beginner-friendly yet concrete, focusing on real-world latency under load.

## Key Concepts
- Cache-aside pattern
- TTL tuning and backoff
- Cache stampede protection (distributed locks)
- Observability: hit rate, latency, QPS
- Failure modes and fallback

## Code Example
```javascript
async function getUser(id){
  const cacheKey = `user:${id}`;
  let v = await redis.get(cacheKey);
  if (v) return JSON.parse(v);
  const lockKey = `lock:${cacheKey}`;
  const acquired = await redis.set(lockKey, '1', { NX: true, PX: 2000 });
  if (!acquired){
    await sleep(50);
    return getUser(id);
  }
  const row = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id=$1', [id]);
  await redis.set(cacheKey, JSON.stringify(row), 'EX', 300);
  await redis.del(lockKey);
  return row;
}
```

